        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "50bd53ae-1e29-5c37-b0fa-bfca20672b90",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Pearcy, Alexander O'Neal, Al Pitrelli, Hiro Kuretani\n- Bands: Ratt, Vertex, Arcade, Vicious Delite, Nitronic, Danger Danger, Hotshot, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, Trans-Siberian Orchestra, WXXI, Trancentral Station\n- Roles: musician, singer, songwriter, arranger, guitarist, drummer, founder\n- Songs: \"Nobody Rides For Free\"\n- Places: Natchez, Mississippi\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander O'Neal was born on November 15, 1953, and he is an American R&B singer, songwriter, and arranger from Natchez, Mississippi.\n- Stephen Eric Pearcy was born on July 3, 1956, and he is an American musician known as Stephen Pearcy.\n- In 1995, the band Vertex was formed featuring singer Stephen Pearcy, guitarist Al Pitrelli, and drummer Hiro Kuretani.\n- Stephen Pearcy is best known as the founder, singer, and songwriter of the heavy metal band Ratt.\n- Al Pitrelli was associated with Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, and Trans-Siberian Orchestra before or alongside Vertex.\n- Hiro Kuretani was associated with WXXI and Trancentral Station before or alongside Vertex.\n- Stephen Pearcy was associated with Ratt, Arcade, Vicious Delite, and Nitronic before or alongside Vertex.\n- \"Nobody Rides For Free\" was a single by the American heavy metal band Ratt.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
